WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Hello Steve

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.700
I’m so glad to be speaking with you

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.220
During my English learning process

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.060
I have this small confusion

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.720
that I wish to resolve today with your help

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.260
As the base of language learning, vocabulary is very important

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.400
However, for many students

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.200
vocabulary is often the most challenging part

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.580
So I would like to ask you

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.515
that in the learning process

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.280
how does one master vocabulary better and faster?

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.360
How to learn vocabulary better and faster

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.120
There is no fast process in language learning

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.960
Learning a new language

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.960
is us getting used to a new language gradually

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.900
This is a slow process

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.160
because our brain needs to get used to the new language

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.520
So you are right

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:54.560
Vocabulary is the most importing part of learning a new language

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.480
because without vocabulary

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.900
you don’t have words

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.660
you can’t express what you want to say

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.040
and you can’t understand a lot of things that you see or hear

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.660
But there is no fast approach

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.000
Only by

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.540
listening to a lot of things and reading a lot of things

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.320
and letting your brain get used to new vocabulary gradually

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.140
such as new phrases and new words

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.380
then you can master new vocabulary

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.460
This process will certainly happen

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.120
and you need to trust your brain

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.280
It needs to have enough stimulation

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.340
and you need to read enough material

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.100
especially things that interest you

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.760
Don’t memorize words or a word list

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.720
that won’t work

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.500
You need to read more and listen to more things that you are interested in

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.220
and try to read out the things that you listen to as well

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.580
In this way, your brain will slowly get used to the new language

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.260
including the new vocabulary

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.460
Hope this will answer your question

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.220
First of all, thank you for giving me this opportunity to speak with you

00:02:09.225 --> 00:02:12.185
I have two questions that I would like to ask from you

00:02:12.185 --> 00:02:15.680
First question, when expressing in a new language

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.640
I sometimes would use English that has been translated directly from Chinese

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.740
then my expression would become not so native

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.200
so I would like to ask you

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.700
if there is a good way to

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.620
improve the language sense of my expression

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.480
and its logic

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.300
When learning a foreign language

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:37.420
we tend to translate it from our mother language

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.320
How do we avoid this?

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.640
Well, it is inevitable

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.640
For Chinese people, when learning a new language, such as English

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.860
they need to get used to it more in order to master it better

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.135
After seeing and listening to a lot of things

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.840
they may have more opportunities to speak

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.395
Slowly, you will not rely on your mother language

00:02:56.395 --> 00:02:59.325
to express what you want to say

00:02:59.325 --> 00:03:02.025
You will then more and more

00:03:02.025 --> 00:03:06.120
express yourself in English directly

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.900
There is no special approach to that

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.480
You just need to carry on with the listening, reading and speaking

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.420
in order to get used a new language gradually

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.080
Then this situation where you have to translate your mother language into a  foreign language

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.200
will likely to happen less and less

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.220
Second question, when expressing in a new language

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.280
I would sometimes try to show my fluency of the language

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.220
and I would speak too fast, but not so clear

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.420
I wonder if you have any good suggestion to this issue

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.120
Thank you

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.300
In regard to the speed of speaking

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.040
there are two situations

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.120
One is when a student

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.620
is trying to show his/her fluency

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.220
then he/she might speak too fast

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.400
In my opinion, when learning a foreign language

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.300
especially on an entry or intermediate level

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.660
you shouldn’t speak too fast

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.680
instead, take it slow

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.500
you need to adapt a speed that you can maintain

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.360
in order to make the other person feels comfortable

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.260
When the other person speaks too fast

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.280
you may not be able to catch all

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.040
but you still need to try to listen

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.500
This is all about letting your brain get used to the new language

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.060
Hope this will answer your question

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.400
First question is how to correct my own pronunciation

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.620
Because sometimes when I’m speaking English

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.920
I would notice that my pronunciation isn’t accurate

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.220
or that my expression isn’t as native

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.020
So how do I speak like a native speaker?

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.640
How to improve your pronunciation

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.960
and speak like a native speaker

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:56.340
First, it is nearly impossible to speak like a native speaker

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:02.260
I do business with many foreigners using English

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.720
and almost no one

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.920
not only Chinese and Japanese

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.540
but German and Swede as well

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.020
They all had an accent

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.220
This is not a problem

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.500
The problem is that you need to make the other person feel comfortable

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.100
especially people whose mother language is English

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.420
You need to make them understand you fully

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.560
So this issue

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.440
is actually about choosing words

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.840
Your ability of choosing the right words is more important than your pronunciation

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.455
I know people who speak English

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.920
by making choice of words

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.240
They can speak very well by choosing the right words

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:37.060
This is a smart move

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.420
Even if they have an accent

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.480
or a heavy pronunciation

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.400
it wouldn’t be a problem

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:46.560
And if you still want to improve your pronunciation

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.740
you need to listen more

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.320
but there are some pronunciations that we didn’t notice

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.120
In English, for example

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.180
bird, b-i-r-d

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.580
heard h-e-a-r-d

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.260
There are words in English

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.320
whose spellings are different for the same pronunciation

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.040
so you need to notice it

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.080
notice those English pronunciations

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.300
and understand them

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.520
then you will most likely

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.960
pronounce them in the right way

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.380
a way that’s close to a native speaker

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.820
So listen more, let your brain get used to it

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:26.540
and notice what happens when you pronounce words

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.160
take it slow, because this can’t be a fast process

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:34.380
You can’t learn a language today and master it tomorrow

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.860
you need to take it slow

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.300
speak more and try not to care too much about your pronunciation

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.660
pay attention to it while listening

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.540
then your pronunciation will slowly get better

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.720
Also, you need to pay attention to your intonation

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:48.860
that is your tone

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.720
Chinese have four tones right?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.900
I need to learn these four tones when learning Chinese

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:54.880
mā má mǎ mà

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.020
English has it too

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.540
You need to pay attention to intonation

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.100
intonation is the music of language

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.920
If you can understand and imitate well

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.200
then your pronunciation will be better

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:10.220
Second question is that when you are practising your hearing

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.460
you may not hear clearly or understand fully

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:17.520
so how to improve English listening ability

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.740
of course, there are more ways to it, for example when I learn a foreign language

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.380
such as Arabic and Persian

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.340
sometimes I still can’t understand after listening to it so many times

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.920
this is normal

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.380
some parts you can listen and understand clearly

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.560
and some parts you can’t

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.740
you just need to carry on

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:37.700
besides, you need to be able to see and read what you hear

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.920
note the words that you don't understand

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.000
especially the compound words

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.080
If you use our LingQ

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.240
Note those words before you reply

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.340
so the parts that you can’t understand easily

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.120
get noticed

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.540
and then you listen to it again, read it again, and listen to it again

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.900
slowly, you will pay more attention to it

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.540
and then slowly

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.820
your hearing will be improved

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.900
Okay, thank you.

